/E (Solidity isahigh-levelprogramming language used to develop smart contracts on blockchain platforms such as Ethereum.Asmartcontract is a program stored on the blockchain that automatically executes predefinedoperations.Solidity supports variables, functions, control statements, data structures, modifiers,andconstructors,which make it suitable for developing decentralized applications. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
78 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (A Solidityprogramgenerally contains an SPDX license identifier, pragma statement, and contract definition.Thepragmastatement specifies the compiler version, while the contract contains state variablesandfunctions.Solidity provides primitive data types such as uint, int, bool, address, string,andbytes.Statevariables are stored permanently on the blockchain, whereas local variables exist onlyduringfunctionexecution. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
79 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (Functionsareusedtoperform operations in a smart contract. A view function can read contract state but cannot modifyit,whileapure function neither reads nor modifies blockchain state. Functions can accept inputparametersandreturn output values. Solidity also provides visibility levels such as public, private, internal, and external to control access to functions and variables. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
80 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (Modifiers are reusable code blocks used to control the execution of functions, commonly for access control. A constructor is executed only once during contract deployment and is generally used to initialize contract variables. Solidity also supports control-flow statements such as if-else, for, while, and do-while for implementing decisions and repeated operations. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
81 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (Solidity provides important data structures such as arrays, mappings, structures, and enums. Arrays store collections of elements, mappings store key-value pairs, structs group related data, and enums represent a predefined set of values. Solidity also uses three major data locations: storage, which stores data permanently on the blockchain; memory, which stores temporary data during function execution; and calldata, which is temporary and read-only data generally used for external function parameters. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
